xis Z)","kind":"stl","pos":[-125.0,-172.2,40.0],"size":[42.3,39.5,42.3],"model":"models/nema17.stl","color":"#8d939a","shaft":[0,-1,0]},{"id":"W_FL","label":"FL mecanum wheel (left-hand)","kind":"mecanum","pos":[125.0,215.5,40.0],"size":[80.0,31.0,80.0],"hand":"L","color":"#2b2b2b"},{"id":"W_FR","label":"FR mecanum wheel (right-hand)","kind":"mecanum","pos":[125.0,-215.5,40.0],"size":[80.0,31.0,80.0],"hand":"R","color":"#2b2b2b"},{"id":"W_BL","label":"BL mecanum wheel (right-hand)","kind":"mecanum","pos":[-125.0,215.5,40.0],"size":[80.0,31.0,80.0],"hand":"R","color":"#2b2b2b"},{"id":"W_BR","label":"BR mecanum wheel (left-hand)","kind":"mecanum","pos":[-125.0,-215.5,40.0],"size":[80.0,31.0,80.0],"hand":"L","color":"#2b2b2b"},{"id":"R4","label":"UNO R4 WiFi (drawn as an Uno)","kind":"board","pos":[-115.7,86.7,116.8],"size":[74.93,53.34,1.6],"tex":"tex/uno.png","yaw":0,"face":"up","note":"Board spans X \u2212150..\u221281.4, Y +60..+113.3. Motor leads reach all four sockets from inboard. USB-C faces \u2212X. Jumpers: D12 + D13 on the A header, caps on MS1 + MS3 under each driver (1/32), EN/GND open. Drivers in with EN on EN. Servos run from the PCA9685 on the shield's SDA/SCL comms header (wiring sheet 3)."},{"id":"SHIELD","label":"CNC Shield v3 + DRV8825 \u00d74","kind":"board","pos":[-113.7,86.7,131.8],"size":[68.58,53.34,1.6],"tex":"tex/cnc.png","yaw":0,"face":"up","note":"Stacked on the R4. Board spans X \u2212150..\u221281.4, Y +60..+113.3. Motor leads reach all four sockets from inboard. USB-C faces \u2212X. Jumpers: D12 + D13 on the A header, caps on MS1 + MS3 under each driver (1/32), EN/GND open. Drivers in with EN on EN. Servos run from the PCA9685 on the shield's SDA/SCL comms header (wiring sheet 3)."},{"id":"DRV_X","label":"DRV8825 (X)","kind":"board","pos":[-125.98,98.98,142.8],"size":[16.81,21.59,1.2],"tex":"tex/drv8825.png","yaw":90,"face":"up","note":""},{"id":"DRV_Y","label":"DRV8825 (Y)","kind":"board","pos":[-104.6,98.98,142.8],"size":[16.81,21.59,1.2],"tex":"tex/drv8825.png","yaw":90,"face":"up","note":""},{"id":"DRV_Z","label":"DRV8825 (Z)","kind":"board","pos":[-125.98,75.27,142.8],"size":[16.81,21.59,1.2],"tex":"tex/drv8825.png","yaw":90,"face":"up","note":""},{"id":"DRV_A","label":"DRV8825 (A)","kind":"board","pos":[-104.6,75.27,142.8],"size":[16.81,21.59,1.2],"tex":"tex/drv8825.png","yaw":90,"face":"up","note":""},{"id":"PI","label":"Raspberry Pi 4","kind":"board","pos":[-107.5,-88.0,114.8],"size":[87.12,57.93,1.6],"tex":"tex/pi4.png","yaw":180,"face":"up","note":"Spans X \u2212150..\u221265, Y \u2212116..\u221260. USB ports face \u2212X (rear). Powered from the USB bank on USB-C; the fallback is a buck at 5.10 V on PHYSICAL header pins 2/4 (+) and 6 (\u2212), never with the bank connected too."},{"id":"XL4015","label":"XL4015 buck \u2192 5.0 V (drawn as the LM2596 module)","kind":"board","pos":[-44.5,110.5,112.8],"size":[48.01,22.99,1.6],"tex":"tex/lm2596.png","yaw":0,"face":"up","note":"Trim to 5.0 V unloaded. IN from the shield's VMOT/GND screws (second wire each); OUT pads \u2192 the PCA9685's V+/GND terminal, which feeds both servos and the fan."},{"id":"ESP3","label":"ESP32-S3 no.3 csi_rx_udp (drawn as a C3 devkit)","kind":"board","pos":[60.0,120.0,112.8],"size":[25.4,43.88,1.6],"tex":"tex/esp32c3.png","yaw":-90,"face":"up","note":"csi_rx_udp firmware: USB-C from its own small power bank beside it, streams CSI to the Pi hotspot on channel 6. ESP32 #2 (csi_tx) is dropped on a 10 cm stand as far along the wall as the room allows."},{"id":"MLX","label":"MLX90640 thermal array","kind":"board","pos":[114.0,0.0,230.0],"size":[1.6,27.58,17.78],"tex":"tex/mlx90640.png","yaw":0.0,"face":"+x","note":"I2C 0x33 on the Pi's SECOND I2C bus (hardware i2c3 on BCM 4/5: dtoverlay=i2c3,pins_4_5, 400 kHz) so the 1 MHz thermal reads never stall the ToF/servo bus. 55\u00b0 FoV: a person at 4 m fills ~6 pixels tall, a warm blob ~10 \u00b0C above the room. Ribbon runs with the camera USB through the tilt axis."},{"id":"LDL","label":"LD2410C LEFT","kind":"board","pos":[-159.0,50.0,300.0],"size":[1.6,21.99,16.02],"tex":"tex/ld2410.png","yaw":30,"face":"+x","note":"Boresight Z = 300, passes over the camera (top \u2248 222). Walleye found floor-level radar sees nothing \u2014 this height is a compromise to TEST."},{"id":"LDR","label":"LD2410C RIGHT","kind":"board","pos":[-159.0,-50.0,300.0],"size":[1.6,21.99,16.02],"tex":"tex/ld2410.png","yaw":-30,"face":"+x","note":"The pair is an amplitude-comparison direction finder: log(E_left / E_right) at the breathing gate gives bearing (localize.py). Both in 0.2 m gate mode."},{"id":"MIC","label":"INMP441 mic (Adafruit art)","kind":"board","pos":[-142.0,0.0,216.0],"size":[1.6,16.51,12.7],"tex":"tex/i2smic.png","yaw":0.0,"face":"+x","note":""},{"id":"TOF_F","label":"VL53L1X ToF FRONT","kind":"board","pos":[179.0,0.0,81.0],"size":[1.6,27.24,17.78],"tex":"tex/vl53l1x.png","yaw":0.0,"face":"+x","note":"XSHUT \u2192 Pi BCM GPIO 22 (GPIO 4/5 are the thermal array's I2C bus). Both share I2C 0x29 until re-addressed at boot."},{"id":"TOF_R","label":"VL53L1X ToF REAR","kind":"board","pos":[-179.0,0.0,81.0],"size":[1.6,27.24,17.78],"tex":"tex/vl53l1x.png","yaw":0.0,"face":"-x","note":"XSHUT \u2192 Pi BCM GPIO 27 (GPIO 4/5 are the thermal array's I2C bus). Both share I2C 0x29 until re-addressed at boot."},{"id":"LD2450","label":"LD2450 radar (on the Pi UART)","kind":"box","pos":[-159.0,0.0,300.0],"size":[43.0,15.0,3.0],"color":"#1d4f91","note":"Between the two LD2410Cs, 50 mm from each. Its own \u00b160\u00b0 field gives x/y of anything that moves; bench-test whether it reports a still, breathing person. Power one radar at a time first, then all three, and watch for mutual interference. Wired straight to the Pi header's UART (pins 4, 34, 10, 8) \u2014 no adapter."},{"id":"PACK","label":"HOOVO 3S 2200 mAh LiPo","kind":"box","pos":[0.0,0.0,74.8],"size":[75.0,33.8,26.4],"color":"#f5c400","note":"Lowest heavy part \u2192 h_CG. Balance lead tucked beside the pack; the cell alarm is optional."},{"id":"PLUG","label":"Deans pull-plug = E-STOP","kind":"box","pos":[-140.0,-132.0,112.0],"size":[30.0,16.0,12.0],"color":"#c0392b","note":"The pack lead comes up through the rear slot to here. One-handed disconnect from above = the emergency stop."},{"id":"BANK","label":"USB power bank 5 V / 3 A","kind":"box","pos":[0.0,0.0,113.5],"size":[100.0,60.0,15.0],"color":"#5c636a","rounded":true,"note":"USB-C to the Pi. Must deliver 5 V at 3 A. Centred to keep the CG on the axis."},{"id":"BANK2","label":"second power bank \u2014 ESP32 only","kind":"box","pos":[60.0,165.0,119.0],"size":[90.0,26.0,26.0],"color":"#5c636a","rounded":true,"note":"Its only load is the CSI node; nothing else plugs into it."},{"id":"HUB","label":"4-port USB hub","kind":"box","pos":[-95.0,-165.0,112.0],"size":[60.0,30.0,12.0],"color":"#2b2b2b","note":"R4 + the two CP2102 adapters; port 4 free. 0.3 m cable to the Pi."},{"id":"CP1","label":"CP2102 no.1","kind":"box","pos":[-40.0,-160.0,111.0],"size":[16.0,50.0,8.0],"color":"#c0392b","note":"Four wires each to an LD2410C: +5V, GND, TXD, RXD (3V3 stays empty). Label LEFT / RIGHT. The LD2450 needs no adapter: it goes straight onto the Pi header (pins 4, 34, 10, 8)."},{"id":"CP2","label":"CP2102 no.2","kind":"box","pos":[-20.0,-160.0,111.0],"size":[16.0,50.0,8.0],"color":"#c0392b","note":"Four wires each to an LD2410C: +5V, GND, TXD, RXD (3V3 stays empty). Label LEFT / RIGHT. The LD2450 needs no adapter: it goes straight onto the Pi header (pins 4, 34, 10, 8)."},{"id":"FAN","label":"40 mm 5 V fan","kind":"stl","pos":[-115.7,86.7,111.0],"size":[40.0,40.0,10.0],"model":"models/fan40.stl","color":"#222222","note":"Blows down onto the four DRV8825 heatsinks. Fan face at Z \u2248 159."},{"id":"PT","label":"Ceres turret base","kind":"box","pos":[110.0,0.0,99.0],"size":[100.0,60.0,6.0],"color":"#d9d2c5"},{"id":"PCA","label":"PCA9685 servo driver","kind":"board","pos":[30.0,-75.0,112.8],"size":[62.23,25.4,1.6],"tex":"tex/pca9685.p